{{Quote|Did...did you see Lugubrious perform?''"<br />"''Yes. It was quite an act. She had a scaled replica of Jabba's sail barge built&mdash;though it was so gaudy it's hard to believe anything like it had ever existed.|[[G'kolu]] and Teal|<ref name="Legends">''[[The Legends of Luke Skywalker]]''</ref>}}
The '''''Khetanna''''' was an [[LO-KD57]] luxury [[sail barge]] manufactured by [[Ubrikkian Industries]] that was modified to suit the needs of the [[Hutt]] [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]]. After the [[Jedi Knight]] [[Luke Skywalker]] [[Death|killed]] Jabba's pet [[rancor]] [[Pateesa]], the crime lord demanded Skywalker and his companions [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]] be executed at the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]]. The Hutt and his entourage traveled to the pit in ''Khetanna'' in order to view the executions, but the prisoners managed to board the sail barge and kill Jabba, destroying the sail barge as they escaped.

==Characteristics==
[[File:KhetannaInterior-RotJAVA.png|thumb|left|300px|Interior of the ''Khetanna'']]
The ''Khetanna'' was fitted with two large sails that were designed to protect its crew from Tatooine's harsh sunlight. It had a large double [[laser cannon]] mounted on the upper deck and could have several heavy blasters mounted to its guardrails. Inside, there was a large banquet room that Jabba used as an audience chamber for him and his guests. The Hutt also decorated the interior of the barge with a [[Ne Ganna Dateel Jabba|bas relief]] of himself.<ref name="ROTJ" />

==History==
===Republic Era===
At some point, [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]] purchased the ''Khetanna''<ref name="BtPotDS!">''[[Return of the Jedi: Beware the Power of the Dark Side!]]''</ref> from [[Ubrikkian Industries]], with the company's artisans custom-building the barge specifically for Jabba's use.<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]''</ref>

[[File:Octopus_ship_capture.png|thumb|right|300px|''Khetanna'' under attack]]
During the early part of the [[Clone Wars]], the ''Khetanna'' was carrying the Hutt's infant son, [[Rotta]] back to his [[Boba Fett's Palace|palace]]. However, it then came under attack by a [[Trident-class assault ship|''Trident''-class assault ship]] commanded by [[Asajj Ventress]], acting under orders from [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] leader [[Count]] [[Dooku]] and his ally, Jabba's uncle [[Ziro Desilijic Tiure|Ziro]]. The ''Khetanna'' was grabbed by the ship and Rotta was taken by Ventress to [[Teth]]. The sail barge survived the attack.<ref name="TCW (f)">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars (film)|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' film]]</ref>

===Imperial Era===
During the [[Galactic Civil War]] between the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] and the [[Galactic Empire|Empire]], Jabba continued to use the ''Khetanna''. He used it when [[Sith Lord|Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Vader]] [[Assault on Cymoon#Aftermath|visited]] him and used its cannons to massacre a party of [[Tusken Raider]]s.<ref name="SW4:SS4">[[Star Wars (2015) 4|''Star Wars'' (2015) 4]]</ref>

In [[3 ABY]],<ref name="OutlawsDate">{{OutlawsDate}}</ref> [[Bib Fortuna]] hired at least two [[Technician|mechanics]] to work on the ''Khetanna''. The mechanics initially thought they were going to be calibrating the sails but were instead tasked with working on the [[blaster cannon]]s. They were able to ensure they would turn on however since they were not [[weaponsmith/Canon|gunsmiths]] they could not be sure that they would work. One of them later worried that they would be punished for their work but another assured them that they would just check that they turned on and that it would have been worse if they told Jabba that they couldn't do the work.<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>

[[File:Khetanna_boom.png|thumb|left|300px|The destruction of the ''Khetanna'']]
Shortly before the [[Battle of Endor]], [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], [[Jedi Knight]] [[Luke Skywalker]], [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]], [[Chewbacca]], and the [[droid]]s [[C-3PO]] and [[R2-D2]] staged a [[Rescue of Han Solo|rescue attempt]] of [[Han Solo]], who was frozen in [[carbonite]] inside Jabba's palace. However, the attempt ended up failing and Organa was forced to become Jabba's slave, while Skywalker, Solo, and Chewbacca were sentenced to death by being consumed by the [[sarlacc]] in the [[Great Pit of Carkoon]]. Jabba, accompanied by Organa and his entourage, traveled to the pit in the ''Khetanna'' to witness the execution. However, R2-D2, who was still aboard the sail barge, launched [[Luke Skywalker's green lightsaber|Skywalker's lightsaber]] into the air, allowing the [[Jedi]] to catch it and fight back against Jabba's thugs, while Organa went on to kill the Hutt. Skywalker soon managed to board the ''Khetanna'', and after neutralizing the guards on top, told Organa to aim the vessel's main [[blaster cannon]] at the deck. The pair proceeded to swing across to one of the nearby [[Bantha-II cargo skiff|skiffs]] while the cannon fired at the barge, starting a chain-reaction and causing it to explode.<ref name="ROTJ" /> Its remains ended up burying the sarlacc, allowing [[Jawa]]s to scavenge them for their business.<ref name="ALD">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref>

===Legacy===
[[File:KhetannaWreckage-BoBFCh4.png|thumb|right|300px|The wreckage of ''Khetanna'' next to the Great Pit of Carkoon.]]
After the ''Khetanna''{{'s}} destruction, [[Lugubrious Mote]], a performer who claimed she was present during the rescue of Han Solo, had a scaled replica of the vessel created that she used during performances. After seeing Mote perform with the sail barge, a [[Youngling|youth]] named [[Teal]] commented the replica was so gaudy that she found it difficult to believe such a ship had ever existed.<ref name="Legends" /> The remains, mostly picked clean, were still somewhat visible when former [[bounty hunter]] [[Boba Fett]] escaped the sarlacc pit<ref name="Chapter 1">{{BOBF|Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land}}</ref>, and later when he and [[Master Assassin]] [[Fennec Shand]] revisited the pit and killed the sarlacc inside, in a failed attempt to retrieve the former's [[Boba Fett's armor|armor]].<ref name="Chapter 4">{{BOBF|Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
When the [[The Star Wars Trilogy Special Edition|Special Edition]] of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]] was in development, the scene of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']] in which Jabba met Han Solo at [[Mos Eisley]] was restored replacing [[Declan Mulholland]] with a CGI Jabba. As such, artist [[Claudia Mullaly]] pitched an idea of featuring Jabba mobilizing in a miniature version of the ''Khetanna'' with a control column at the bow for steering. However, as incorporating it into the original footage would have been difficult (especially when Solo steps on Jabba), this idea went shelved.<ref name="Mini Khetanna">{{SW|url=news/6-fascinating-behind-the-scenes-concepts-from-the-star-wars-trilogy-special-edition|text=6 Fascinating Behind-the-Scenes Concepts from The ''Star Wars'' Trilogy Special Edition|nolive=1}}</ref>

